{
 "result": "csvsum.py is a single-pass stdin reader: it reads all bytes, replaces commas with spaces, splits into tokens, takes categories as every third token starting at index 4 and values as the following tokens parsed with float, accumulates sums in a dict via dict.get, then writes sorted 'cat,sum' lines with 2-decimal formatting. It passed the samples and was registered with assay at baseline 2.19445 (noise 3.2%). I stopped here with 63 energy because the remaining candidate rewrites were unlikely to beat the baseline by more than the 3.2% noise threshold, and each further step costs 16 to 107 energy.",
